WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.001
SPEAKER:<i> The American embassy</i>

00:00:02.101 --> 00:00:05.037
<i> was like the symbol
 of American imperialism</i>

00:00:05.137 --> 00:00:06.572
right in the center of Tehran.

00:00:06.672 --> 00:00:07.941
(CROWD YELLS)

00:00:08.041 --> 00:00:10.744 line:0%
(SPEAKING FOREIGN LANGUAGE)

00:00:15.881 --> 00:00:16.783
(CROWD CHANTS)

00:00:17.317 --> 00:00:18.918
SPEAKER 2:<i> I go to the window,
 and I look out.</i>

00:00:19.018 --> 00:00:20.853
I see a vast crowd of people.

00:00:21.787 --> 00:00:24.690
<i> The embassy alarm system
 goes off, people are yelling.</i>

00:00:24.791 --> 00:00:26.059
<i> Finally, we just surrendered.</i>

00:00:26.159 --> 00:00:27.059
(CROWD YELLING)

00:00:27.593 --> 00:00:30.363
SPEAKER 3:<i> I gave up my weapon.
 They blindfold me.</i>

00:00:30.797 --> 00:00:32.665
I thought that was it for me.

00:00:32.765 --> 00:00:33.966
♪ (DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYS) ♪

00:00:34.066 --> 00:00:36.335
REPORTER:<i> The American embassy
 in Tehran is in the hands</i>

00:00:36.435 --> 00:00:37.637
<i> of Muslim students tonight.</i>

00:00:38.004 --> 00:00:40.005
REPORTER 2:<i> They're holding
 the Americans hostage.</i>

00:00:40.706 --> 00:00:43.709
It's an extraordinary act
and an audacious act

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:45.411
<i>to humiliate the United States.</i>

00:00:45.511 --> 00:00:48.948
SPEAKER 4:
<i> And it was having a big impact
 on the American public.</i>

00:00:49.415 --> 00:00:51.317
SPEAKER 5:<i> We were helping
 the American people</i>

00:00:51.417 --> 00:00:53.753
<i> to understand
the consequences of the actions</i>

00:00:53.853 --> 00:00:55.321
of their government in Iran.

00:00:55.421 --> 00:00:58.891
SPEAKER 6:
<i>There was an unholy pact between
 the United States and Iran.</i>

00:00:59.358 --> 00:01:01.927
In one word,
the special relationship...

00:01:02.828 --> 00:01:04.397
SPEAKER 7:<i> It seemed to me
 that the oil wealth</i>

00:01:04.497 --> 00:01:07.534
<i> wasn't trickling down
 to the people.</i>

00:01:08.234 --> 00:01:10.136
And that made me very angry.

00:01:10.736 --> 00:01:13.706
SPEAKER 2:
<i> The social fragmentation,
 the corruption.</i>

00:01:13.806 --> 00:01:14.874
<i> That was the fuel.</i>

00:01:14.974 --> 00:01:16.041
Khomeini was the match.

00:01:16.141 --> 00:01:17.877
(CROWD CHANTS)

00:01:17.977 --> 00:01:19.979
The revolution became a monster.

00:01:20.446 --> 00:01:21.914
I thought we were gonna
have freedom.

00:01:22.014 --> 00:01:25.084
They were just absolutely
convinced that we were spies.

00:01:25.184 --> 00:01:27.587
SPEAKER 2:
<i>My interrogation was unpleasant.</i>

00:01:27.687 --> 00:01:28.387
Let's put it that way.

00:01:28.921 --> 00:01:31.357
The hostages have been there
for almost a year now.

00:01:31.457 --> 00:01:32.858
This is gonna be the basis
of this election.

00:01:33.125 --> 00:01:34.593
SPEAKER 8:
<i> This was totally televised.</i>

00:01:34.693 --> 00:01:36.796
<i> And it was very
 television friendly.</i>

00:01:36.896 --> 00:01:40.232
<i> Carter was convinced
 that he could solve this.</i>

00:01:40.599 --> 00:01:44.270
He never dreamed
it would go on 444 days.

00:01:44.837 --> 00:01:48.273
SPEAKER 9:<i> How do you think
 this will all turn out?</i>

00:01:48.374 --> 00:01:50.309
SPEAKER 10:
<i>Why did this go on for so long?</i>

00:01:50.576 --> 00:01:52.779
I never thought of myself
as a hero.

00:01:52.879 --> 00:01:54.380
<i> I wanted to make it home.</i>

